.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBFlexCells\fR: a line of cells sized as CSS flex sizes them. Each cell has a \fBFlex\fR (basis, grow, shrink, minimum), and the line divides its width with \fBlayouts::flex::rule::resolve\fR: free space goes to the cells that grow, a shortage is taken from the cells that shrink in proportion to their basis, and \fBno cell goes below its minimum\fR.
.PP
It is the line of a table: the header and every row are a \fBFlexCells\fR over the same \fBFlex\fR specs, so their columns line up at any width, and a small column keeps what its label needs while a big one gives way ("Tim" never happens). \fBItemRow\fR and \fBSortHeader\fR are built on it.
.PP
.nf
.RS
FlexCells::new()
    .cell(Flex::fixed(40.0), picture)               // never shrinks
    .cell(Flex::grow(1.0, 60.0), title)             // takes the free space, down to 60
    .cell(Flex::shrink(160.0, 80.0), album)         // starts at 160, shrinks to 80
    .cell(Flex::shrink(44.0, 44.0), time)           // keeps its 44
.RE
.fi
